# GLOOM

[![Python](https://img.shields.io/badge/python-3.12%2B-blue)](https://www.python.org/)
[![License: MIT](https://img.shields.io/badge/license-MIT-green.svg)](LICENSE)
[![Status](https://img.shields.io/badge/status-alpha-orange.svg)](#project-status)
[![Domain](https://img.shields.io/badge/domain-bioinformatics-purple.svg)](#overview)

**Gene network Learning and Organization through Optimized Machine intelligence**

GLOOM is a modular Python framework for **lung adenocarcinoma (LUAD) candidate gene prioritization**. It integrates tumor and normal transcriptomic data, differential expression statistics, co-expression network topology, supervised machine learning, pathway enrichment, and interactive reporting into a single reproducible workflow.

The core aim of GLOOM is to move from raw gene-expression matrices to an interpretable ranked list of candidate LUAD-associated genes:

```text
raw RNA-seq data
   -> quality control and harmonization
   -> differential expression analysis
   -> expression and network feature engineering
   -> machine-learning model training
   -> genome-wide gene ranking
   -> novel candidate detection
   -> network export, pathway enrichment, and interactive reports
```

